he flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\left\\langle 2 x^{2} + 4 y, \\; 2 x^{2} + 4 x y \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nthrough the boundary of the region enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2}$ and the lines $y=0$ and $x=1.$" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553757 1072 #uuid "391564c7-a751-5991-b788-dcbb08b27c2c" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553757 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/91/9168d2ed7eeaa5f1dd331a0a986ac7ecfd6b964217a2cb614deb0cdd54437d65.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=2 x^{2} + 4 y$ and $Q(x,y)=2 x^{2} + 4 x y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}=4 x,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}=4 x.\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y):0\\leq x\\leq 1,\\quad 0\\leq y\\leq x^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\oint_C \\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf n\\,ds&=\\oint_C P\\,dy-Q\\,dx \\\\&=\\iint_D\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,dA \\\\&=\\iint_D\\left(8 x\\right)\\,dA \\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{x^{2}}\\left(8 x\\right)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left[8 x y\\right]_{y=0}^{y=x^{2}}\\,dx \\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(8 x^{3}\\right)\\,dx \\\\&=\\left[2 x^{4}\\right]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\&=\\left(2\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553758 1080 "0" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553758 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553758 1083 #uuid "591a446f-82dd-564c-b15f-8e8267e36fdc" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553759 1080 "6" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553759 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553759 1083 #uuid "5a7ef8e8-03eb-5e71-9954-b61f0cd0045d" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553760 1080 "7" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553760 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553760 1083 #uuid "75dd0d96-1827-5799-ba11-bbee875c6ba2" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553758 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553759 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553763 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553765 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553766 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1077 "selection" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1078 #edb/ref 17592186553763 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553761 1079 #uuid "779da836-a9bf-5772-a9db-115da484b79e" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553762 1080 "4" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553762 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553762 1083 #uuid "84167764-9866-593d-9f3f-728b74e99429" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553763 1080 "2" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553763 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553763 1083 #uuid "996ebf57-fd88-5775-876c-167c46de26ee" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553764 1068 #edb/ref 17592186553754 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553764 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553764 1071 "Use the flux form of Green's theorem to calculate the flux of the vector field\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\left\\langle 28 x y, \\; 12 x^{2} y + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nthrough the boundary of the region enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{3}$ and the lines $y=0$ and $x=1.$" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553764 1072 #uuid "9f300428-dd28-5d22-81b0-c450650df73d" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553764 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j,$ and $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then the flux form of Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∬}_{D}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dy-Q\\,dx={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](images/e6/e6f6a5cf9b37fe16f17fe74face946d85b426badf8db710ca4a7ea308a1ff2ec.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=28 x y$ and $Q(x,y)=12 x^{2} y + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}=28 y,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}=12 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y):0\\leq x\\leq 1,\\quad 0\\leq y\\leq x^{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem in flux form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\oint_C \\mathbf F\\cdot\\mathbf n\\,ds&=\\oint_C P\\,dy-Q\\,dx \\\\&=\\iint_D\\left(\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,dA \\\\&=\\iint_D\\left(12 x^{2} + 28 y\\right)\\,dA \\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\int_{0}^{x^{3}}\\left(12 x^{2} + 28 y\\right)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left[12 x^{2} y + 14 y^{2}\\right]_{y=0}^{y=x^{3}}\\,dx \\\\&=\\int_{0}^{1}\\left(x^{5} \\left(14 x + 12\\right)\\right)\\,dx \\\\&=\\left[2 x^{7} + 2 x^{6}\\right]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\&=\\left(4\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\&=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553765 1080 "4" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553765 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553765 1083 #uuid "aab019ae-93c7-50b3-9811-d455898d1942" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553766 1080 "8" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553766 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553766 1083 #uuid "cc2ac1da-5902-5d50-a8d4-5ac0daceec12" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553767 1080 "10" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553767 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553767 1083 #uuid "d900e075-bbea-5147-aeda-64c204455c22" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553768 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186172099.py" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true] [17592186553768 1169 #uuid "ae8aeed1-6e4f-5d6d-bd4f-c30d442a97bc" 13194139535991 17592186045443 true]] :edb/tempids {"05ec21ed-67a9-5f57-8257-9837d31fa900" 17592186553754 "193c7f3f-1b13-52cf-b99e-2cb82e2ec402" 17592186553755 "30eb9b0a-3b5c-550c-97df-45c92636de58" 17592186553756 "391564c7-a751-5991-b788-dcbb08b27c2c" 17592186553757 "591a446f-82dd-564c-b15f-8e8267e36fdc" 17592186553758 "5a7ef8e8-03eb-5e71-9954-b61f0cd0045d" 17592186553759 "75dd0d96-1827-5799-ba11-bbee875c6ba2" 17592186553760 "779da836-a9bf-5772-a9db-115da484b79e" 17592186553761 "84167764-9866-593d-9f3f-728b74e99429" 17592186553762 "996ebf57-fd88-5775-876c-167c46de26ee" 17592186553763 "9f300428-dd28-5d22-81b0-c450650df73d" 17592186553764 "aab019ae-93c7-50b3-9811-d455898d1942" 17592186553765 "cc2ac1da-5902-5d50-a8d4-5ac0daceec12" 17592186553766 "d900e075-bbea-5147-aeda-64c204455c22" 17592186553767 "generator" 17592186553768}}
